content.text:
The `GET /api/v1/bookmarks/search?q=term` endpoint has been implemented:

### 1. Service Search Method (`src/services/bookmark-service.ts`)
```ts
search(query: string): Bookmark[] {
  const trimmed = query.trim();
  if (!trimmed) {
    return [];
  }
  const lower = trimmed.toLowerCase();
  return this.getAll().filter((bookmark) => {
    const titleMatch =
      bookmark.title !== undefined &&
      bookmark.title.toLowerCase().includes(lower);
    const tagMatch =
      bookmark.tags !== undefined &&
      bookmark.tags.some(
        (tag) => tag.toLowerCase() === lower || tag === trimmed
      );
    return titleMatch || tagMatch;
  });
}
```

### 2. Route Implementation (`src/routes/bookmarks.ts`)
- Mounted `GET /search` before `GET /:id` to ensure proper Express route precedence.
- Validates that `q` is a non-empty string; responds with HTTP 400 (`{ error: 'Search query parameter "q" is required and cannot be empty' }`) if missing or whitespace.
- Calls `bookmarkService.search(q)` and returns HTTP 200 with the matching bookmarks array.

### 3. Verification & Tests
- Added tests in `tests/bookmarks.test.ts`, `src/services/bookmark-service.test.ts`, and `tests/bookmark-service.test.ts` covering:
  - Case-insensitive substring match on `title`.
  - Exact match on `tags`.
  - Empty array when no matches exist.
  - HTTP 400 when `q` is absent or whitespace.
- All 86 tests pass (`vitest run`).
- Strict TypeScript check (`tsc --noEmit`) passes with 0 errors and zero `any` usage.

